// An ungerminated seed, and a `Powder` on purpose: seeds fall.
//
// Previously a seed was `wood` (Plant kind), which never moves, so one
// placed in mid-air hung there and germinated into a tree growing out of
// nothing. Reported from live play as "seeds stay where placed and do not
// drop... hard to place on the soil surface and unrealistic".
//
// Being a Powder means it falls, rolls down slopes, piles in hollows and
// comes to rest on the surface -- all of it from the CA rules that already
// exist, with no seed-specific movement code anywhere. It also means seeds
// scattered over uneven ground collect where real seeds collect.
//
// `Germinate` converts the landed cell to `wood` (plant.rs's `germinate`),
// so this material only ever exists before germination.
(
    name: "seed",
    display: "Seed",
    kind: Powder,
    // Light: a seed sinks through water rather than floating, but only
    // just.
    density: 0.6,
    // Steep, so seeds sit where they land instead of running like sand to
    // the bottom of every slope. Real seeds are irregular and interlock.
    // **Lowering this was tried, measured and reverted -- do not retry it
    // as a reseeding fix.** 55 gives `roll_reach_at` 0.70 cells and
    // `stability_reach_at` 0.51, so a seed at rest can look less than one
    // cell along the surface, and the obvious reading is that a seed which
    // lands on a leaf or on the pile of its siblings can never move again.
    // That reading is right about the mechanism and wrong about the remedy.
    //
    // Measured in an isolated worktree, one founder, herb, 60,000 frames,
    // `reseed_probe launch=0`, three arms built from three clean trees:
    //
    //   repose 55, no canopy fall   1,446 borne ->    82 germ,  37 alive, 141 cols
    //   repose 55, canopy fall on   2,680 borne -> 1,291 germ, 120 alive, 330 cols
    //   repose 22, canopy fall on   2,633 borne ->   702 germ, 120 alive, 315 cols
    //
    // So `falls_through_organisms` is the entire effect and 22 **halves** it
    // -- the seed reaches the floor either way once it can fall through a
    // canopy, and rolling it further only carries it off the damp patch it
    // landed on. It also cost `a_spread_leaf_cluster_is_longer_than_a_blob`,
    // and the mechanism first blamed for that (a founding seed rolling to a
    // different column) was measured and **refuted**: at world seed 11 the
    // founder germinates at (100, 60) at both settings, because
    // `plant_tree_on_ground` packs soil on every side of the spawn point and
    // there is nothing to roll down.
    friction_angle: 55.0,
    colors: [
        (126, 96, 52),
        (142, 110, 62),
        (110, 84, 44),
        (156, 122, 70),
    ],
    // Burns easily and briefly, like the dry husk it is.
    // **And it falls past a branch rather than sitting on it.** The same
    // 2D-slice rule `MaterialDef::falls_through_organisms` states as data,
    // and `windfall.ron`'s argument for it applies here a fortiori: a
    // windfall is a fruit, this is the bare seed inside one, and if
    // anything it is smaller and rounder. A one-cell-wide branch in this
    // slice is not a shelf spanning the wood's whole depth.
    //
    // **It was set on the fruit and missed on the seed, and that omission
    // is most of why nothing spreads.** Measured, `reseed_probe founders=1
    // species=herb frames=60000`: of the ~200 seeds standing at any moment
    // **157 were resting on plant tissue**, and the germination gate can
    // never open on one of those -- it wants `water_capacity > 0` directly
    // underneath and living tissue has none. So a plant's own canopy is
    // where its seed goes to expire, while the fruit form of the same seed
    // reaches the floor.
    //
    // The density argument runs the other way here exactly as it does on
    // `windfall`, and is not the criterion: this is 0.6 against
    // `deadwood`'s 0.7, and deadwood deliberately *does* hang up in a
    // crown.
    falls_through_organisms: true,
    flammability: 0.5,
    burn_temperature: 500.0,
    burn_duration: 30,
    burns_into: "ash",
    heat_conductivity: 0.15,

    // Concentrated plant matter. Same value as leaf for now; a seed
    // being worth more than a leaf is a real distinction and wants a
    // measurement, not a guess.
    food_energy: 480.0,
    // In MPa like every other value of this field. The hard part of plant
    // matter is the coat and the rind, not the flesh; level with `snow`.
    penetration_resistance: 0.2,
    food_class: -1.0,
)
